===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[daylight]]|daylights|daylighting|daylighted|past2=daylit}}

# To expose to daylight
#* '''1895''', {{w|H. G. Wells}}, ''{{w|The Time Machine}}'', Chapter 7, [http://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/35/pg35-images.html]
#*: {{...}} the Morlocks, subterranean for innumerable generations, had come at last to find the '''daylit''' surface intolerable.
#* '''1953''', {{w|C. S. Lewis}}, ''{{w|The Silver Chair}}'', Collins, 1998, Chapter 15,
#*: {{...}} she was not looking at the '''daylit''', sunny world which she so wanted to see.
# {{lb|en|architecture}} To provide sources of natural illumination such as [[skylight]]s or windows.
# To allow light in, as by opening [[drapes]].
# {{lb|en|landscaping|civil engineering}} To run a drainage pipe to an opening from which its contents can drain away naturally.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To gain exposure to the open.
#: ''The seam of coal '''daylighted''' at a cliff by the river.''

